From a8d2c7cf7a999a661926d950d2c192076b8da093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Kroll <t.kroll@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:20:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Renew the slicer CRL automatically

Bambu issues CRLs valid for one month and the printer refuses
app_cert_install with an expired one, so signed control stopped working
after a month without manual renewal.

Every 12 hours, once the installed CRL expires within 10 days, fetch the
certificate URL stored in .storage/bambu_lab/slicer_refresh/<serial>.url
(the request the networking plugin makes on startup), validate the
response and write it into the entry options; the reload installs it on
the printer. The CRL must be signed by the returned chain, currently
valid, newer than the installed one and must not revoke our leaf. The
key is only replaced when the leaf rotated and must match it (cipher
ported from BambuKeySaver, MIT). Without a URL or when renewal fails, a
persistent notification warns from 7 days before expiry. Errors are
logged by type only, because aiohttp messages contain the URL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
